BT /F1 11 Tf 48 790 Td (- No single client can exceed their configured quota) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 774 Td (- Throttled requests receive a clear `429` response within 5ms) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 758 Td (- Legitimate traffic at or below quota is never rejected) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 742 Td (- Rate limit rules can be changed by operations without a service restart) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 712 Td (---) Tj /F1 12 Tf 48 682 Td (BO-2 · Eliminate duplicate payment charges) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 653 Td (Guarantee that a payment is processed exactly once, regardless of how many times the client) Tj (submits the same request due to network retries or timeouts.) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 609 Td (**Acceptance Criteria:**) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 593 Td (- Submitting the same `Idempotency-Key` within 24 hours returns the original result with no) Tj (new DB record created) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 563 Td (- Zero duplicate entries in the `payments` table under any retry scenario) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 547 Td (- Zero double-charge incidents in load and integration testing) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 517 Td (---) Tj /F1 12 Tf 48 487 Td (BO-3 · Centralise and standardise client verification) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 458 Td (Provide a single, secure OTP service that all downstream systems use for client identity) Tj (verification, with consistent security policies and a unified audit trail.) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 414 Td (**Acceptance Criteria:**) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 398 Td (- All OTP generation and verification flows through rate-sentinel exclusively) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 382 Td (- OTP never stored in plaintext in any system) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 366 Td (- Lockout policy \(attempts, duration\) is centrally configurable without code changes) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 350 Td (- All OTP events \(generate, verify, fail, lock\) are auditable from a single source) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 320 Td (---) Tj /F1 12 Tf 48 290 Td (BO-4 · Decouple business logic from notification delivery) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 261 Td (Allow business services to publish notification intent without owning vendor credentials,) Tj (retry logic, or delivery state. The platform absorbs all communication complexity behind a) Tj (Kafka contract.) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 203 Td (**Acceptance Criteria:**) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 187 Td (- Downstream services publish a `NotificationEvent` to Kafka with zero knowledge of the) Tj (delivery vendor) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 157 Td (- Adding a new communication channel requires no changes to any business service) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 141 Td (- All notification events published by this platform are consumed and delivered by message-) Tj (relay) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 97 Td (---) Tj /F1 13 Tf 48 67 Td (5. Business Rules) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
