BT /F1 12 Tf 48 776 Td (BR-1 · OTP must never be stored in plaintext) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 747 Td (Customer verification codes are sensitive credentials. Storing them in plaintext exposes) Tj (customers to credential theft if the database is compromised.) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 703 Td (- OTPs must be BCrypt-hashed \(work factor ? 10\) immediately upon generation) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 687 Td (- The plaintext OTP must be discarded after hashing; it must never appear in any database) Tj (column, log line, or API response) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 657 Td (- Only the hash is persisted; verification uses `BCryptPasswordEncoder.matches\(\)`) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 627 Td (---) Tj /F1 12 Tf 48 597 Td (BR-2 · Payment idempotency window is 24 hours) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 568 Td (Client retries are expected within a session window but must not persist indefinitely.) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 538 Td (- An `Idempotency-Key` submitted more than 24 hours after the original request is treated as) Tj (a new transaction) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 508 Td (- Redis TTL on idempotency keys must be exactly 24 hours) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 492 Td (- MySQL acts as the durable secondary guard against Redis eviction edge cases) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 462 Td (---) Tj /F1 12 Tf 48 432 Td (BR-3 · Locked accounts must not receive new OTPs) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 403 Td (Allowing OTP generation while an account is locked circumvents the brute-force protection) Tj (mechanism.) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 359 Td (- `POST /api/otp/generate` must return `400 Bad Request` with a "locked" message for any) Tj (identifier in Redis lockout state) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 329 Td (- Lockout is applied per `identifier + otpType` combination, not globally per identifier) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 313 Td (- Lockout duration and max attempts are externally configurable without code changes) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 283 Td (---) Tj /F1 12 Tf 48 253 Td (BR-4 · Rate limit rules take effect within one request cycle) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 224 Td (Business decisions to restrict a client must be enforceable immediately without service) Tj (downtime.) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 180 Td (- A rule update via `PUT /api/admin/rules/{id}` must evict the Redis cache synchronously) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 164 Td (- The next incoming request after the update must use the new rule, not the old cached value) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 148 Td (- Total time from API call to rule enforcement must be under 1 second) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 118 Td (---) Tj /F1 12 Tf 48 88 Td (BR-5 · All secrets managed through Azure Key Vault) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 59 Td (No sensitive credentials may appear in version-controlled files or environment variables in) Tj (production.) Tj ET
endstream
