BT /F1 11 Tf 48 776 Td (Checkmarx One free-tier scan must be configured as a required CI step. Builds must fail on) Tj (any critical or high-severity finding.) Tj /F1 12 Tf 48 732 Td (SC-2 · No hardcoded credentials) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 703 Td (Zero tolerance for passwords, API keys, or JWT secrets in source code or configuration files) Tj (committed to version control.) Tj /F1 12 Tf 48 659 Td (SC-3 · PII protection in logs) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 630 Td (Phone numbers and email addresses must never appear unmasked in application logs. Log) Tj (statements must use masked versions only.) Tj /F1 12 Tf 48 586 Td (SC-4 · Brute-force protection on OTP) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 557 Td (Maximum 3 failed verify attempts before account lockout. Lockout must be enforced at the) Tj (Redis layer \(not application layer\) to survive application restarts.) Tj /F1 12 Tf 48 513 Td (SC-5 · Input validation on all endpoints) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 484 Td (All request parameters must be validated before processing. Malformed input returns `400 Bad) Tj (Request` with a descriptive error message. No stack traces exposed to callers.) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 440 Td (---) Tj /F1 13 Tf 48 410 Td (9. Operational Requirements) Tj /F1 12 Tf 48 378 Td (OR-1 · Zero-downtime rule updates) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 349 Td (Platform operators must be able to update rate limit rules, add new clients, and change) Tj (thresholds without restarting the service or causing any request failures during the update.) Tj /F1 12 Tf 48 305 Td (OR-2 · Single-command local environment) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 276 Td (A new engineer must be able to run the complete platform locally using `docker-compose up) Tj (-d` followed by `./mvnw spring-boot:run` ? no additional infrastructure setup required.) Tj /F1 12 Tf 48 232 Td (OR-3 · Health and readiness endpoints) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 203 Td (`/actuator/health` must return system health including Redis and MySQL connectivity.) Tj (`/actuator/health/readiness` must signal when the application is ready to accept traffic.) Tj (Both used by Kubernetes liveness and readiness probes.) Tj /F1 12 Tf 48 145 Td (OR-4 · Structured log format) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 116 Td (All log output must follow a consistent structured pattern: `timestamp | thread | level |) Tj (logger | message`. Logs must include `clientId` and `correlationId` in every line related to) Tj (a business transaction for distributed tracing.) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 58 Td (---) Tj ET
