BT /F1 11 Tf 48 790 Td (|---|---|---|---|---|) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 774 Td (| R-01 | Redis failure takes down rate limiter and OTP entirely | Medium | High | Redis) Tj (Sentinel in prod; graceful degradation to allow-all with Sentry alert |) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 744 Td (| R-02 | Kafka broker outage blocks all notification dispatch | Low | High | Replication) Tj (factor ? 2; producer retries with `acks=all`; consumer lag alerting |) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 714 Td (| R-03 | JWT secret rotation causes all active sessions to invalidate | Low | Medium | Key) Tj (rotation procedure documented; rolling restart with overlapping validity window |) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 684 Td (| R-04 | MySQL connection pool exhaustion under payment burst | Medium | Medium | HikariCP) Tj (pool tuning; connection pool metrics exposed to Prometheus |) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 654 Td (| R-05 | Idempotency key collision across different clients | Very Low | High | Key) Tj (namespaced by `clientId` at lookup level; collision structurally impossible |) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 610 Td (---) Tj /F1 13 Tf 48 580 Td (14. Glossary) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 548 Td (| Term | Definition |) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 532 Td (|---|---|) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 516 Td (| Idempotency Key | A client-supplied UUID that uniquely identifies a payment intent, used) Tj (to prevent duplicate processing on retry |) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 486 Td (| Rate Limit Rule | A database-backed configuration defining the request limit, time window,) Tj (and algorithm for a specific client-route combination |) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 456 Td (| OTP | One-Time Password ? a time-limited numeric code used to verify client identity via) Tj (SMS, email, or WhatsApp |) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 426 Td (| Sliding Window | A rate-limiting algorithm that counts requests within a rolling time) Tj (window using a Redis sorted set |) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 396 Td (| Token Bucket | A rate-limiting algorithm that models a bucket of tokens replenished at a) Tj (fixed rate; each request consumes one token |) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 366 Td (| NotificationEvent | The Kafka message payload published by rate-sentinel containing the) Tj (recipient, channel, template, and priority for a notification |) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 336 Td (| DLQ | Dead Letter Queue ? a Kafka topic that receives messages that could not be) Tj (successfully delivered after all retry attempts |) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 306 Td (| SAST | Static Application Security Testing ? automated code scanning for security) Tj (vulnerabilities, performed by Checkmarx |) Tj /F1 11 Tf 48 276 Td (| PII | Personally Identifiable Information ? data such as phone numbers and email addresses) Tj (that must be protected under data privacy regulations |) Tj ET
endstream
